        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"company_description\": \"Large retail company operating in Europe.\",\n  \"headquarters\": \"Karlsruhe, Germany\",\n  \"approximate_employees\": 50000,\n  \"employee_count_source_note\": \"Approximate current figure from retrieved sources\",\n  \"products_services\": [\"Retail\", \"Consumer goods\"],\n  \"geographic_presence\": \"Germany and several European markets\",\n  \"legal_regulatory_reputational_issues\": [],\n  \"source_urls\": [\"https://example.com/source\"]\n}",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You extract company facts ONLY from the Tavily search response supplied to you. Do not use your own background knowledge. Do not invent or estimate facts that are absent from the retrieved results.\\n\\nRules:\\n- company_description: concise factual description based only on retrieved evidence.\\n- headquarters: return \"Unknown\" if not supported.\\n- approximate_employees: return a whole number if a credible approximate employee count is supported; otherwise return 0.\\n- employee_count_source_note: briefly state what the retrieved result says, or \"Unknown\".\\n- products_services: list main products/services supported by retrieved results.\\n- geographic_presence: concise description of countries/regions supported by retrieved results, or \"Unknown\".\\n- legal_regulatory_reputational_issues: include only significant, publicly documented issues surfaced in the retrieved results. Phrase neutrally and factually. If none surfaced, return an empty list; do NOT claim that none exist globally.\\n- source_urls: include the most relevant retrieved URLs.\\n\\nNever call a company 'shady' and never infer wrongdoing."
        }
      },
