    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Write a concise professional B2B follow-up email for this trade fair lead.\n\nUse ONLY the information below. Do not invent facts.\n\nContact name:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.contact_name }}\n\nCompany:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.company_name }}\n\nRole:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.role }}\n\nTraining needs:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.training_needs.join(', ') }}\n\nPain points:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.pain_points.join(', ') }}\n\nConversation summary:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.notes_summary }}\n\nRequested follow-up:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.requested_follow_up }}\n\nRecommended next step:\n{{ $('Calculate Score + Build Report').item.json.recommended_next_step }}\n\nInstructions:\n- Write only the email body.\n- Do not write a subject line.\n- Keep it around 80-140 words.\n- Be friendly, professional and concise.\n- Refer to one concrete topic discussed with the lead.\n- Include one relevant talking point based on their training need or pain point.\n- Suggest a simple next step.\n- Avoid aggressive or exaggerated sales language.\n- Never mention the lead score.\n- Never mention AI.\n- Do not invent names, dates, products or promises.\n- If the contact name is \"Unknown\", use a neutral greeting such as \"Hello,\".\n- Use the language of the lead notes if it is clear. Otherwise use English.",
